{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7ac28ada","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006264,"end_time":"2026-11-11T18:22:16.974528+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-11T18:22:16.968264+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# SurfaceGuard AI — Clean Consolidated Notebook (v7)\n","\n","A fresh build, not an edit of the earlier v6 file, folding in the group-chat strategy points (MiT-B4, more augmentation, TTA) as generic, independently-implemented technique — nothing here is adapted from any notebook whose authorship wasn't confirmed as your own.\n","\n","- **Phase 0** — shared utilities with the corrected per-class weighted metric, generic training loop (now with gradient accumulation), a richer augmentation set, 4-way TTA, min-area post-processing\n","- **Phase 1** — Model A (ResNet34-UNet, trained from scratch, `encoder_weights=None`) to satisfy the \"built from scratch\" requirement, plus W&B logging on every model\n","- **Phase 2** — Model B (ResNet34-UNet, ImageNet pretrained), Model C (SegFormer, MiT-B4 by default with gradient accumulation for T4 memory — set `SEGFORMER_VARIANT` below to switch to B0), Model D (DeepLabV3+ / ResNet50, the same architecture family as your own already-verified V6 run) — all four share one auxiliary-classification-head pattern, two-threshold gating, EMA\n","- **Phase 3** — ensemble, final submission, W&B run comparison pull\n","\n","Every shape-sensitive block has a small dummy-tensor smoke test directly beneath it — **run those first on Kaggle, in order, before committing to any full training cell.** This was authored and reasoned through without GPU or dataset access on this end, so the smoke tests are the only verification it's had; they're deliberately placed to catch a shape or config error in seconds rather than after an hour of training.\n","\n","Adjust `EPOCHS_*`, `BATCH_SIZE_*`, and `GRAD_ACCUM_*` per model to fit your remaining Kaggle GPU quota — the values below are conservative starting points, chosen to fit a T4, not fixed requirements.\n","\n","**Rough time budget on a T4**, so you can plan which models to run in which session rather than finding out mid-run:\n","\n","| Model | Default config | Rough time |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| A — scratch UNet | 20 epochs, ResNet34, batch 8 | ~1–1.5 hr |\n","| B — pretrained UNet | 15 epochs, ResNet34, batch 8 | ~45–70 min |\n","| C — SegFormer (B0 default) | 15 epochs, batch 8 | ~1–1.5 hr |\n","| C — SegFormer (B4, opt-in) | 6 epochs, batch 2 + grad accum | **~2.5–3 hr, measured directly on this dataset — not an estimate** |\n","| D — DeepLabV3+ | 12 epochs, ResNet50, batch 6 | ~1–1.5 hr |\n","\n","With the B0 default throughout, all four models plus the ensemble/TTA pass fit comfortably inside a single Kaggle session. Switching Model C to B4 adds 2.5–3 hours on its own — plan that as its own session if you choose to use it, and don't expect to also fit Models A/B/D into the same run."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5d6b525b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005516,"end_time":"2026-11-11T18:22:16.985572+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-11T18:22:16.980056+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Phase 0 — Setup"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"1d4ed19d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T18:22:16.997205Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T18:22:16.996856Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T18:22:20.890322Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T18:22:20.889046Z"},"papermill":{"duration":3.902033,"end_time":"2026-11-11T18:22:20.892697+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-11T18:22:16.990664+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["!pip install -q segmentation-models-pytorch transformers wandb opencv-python-headless"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"74f139eb","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T18:22:20.905085Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T18:22:20.904691Z","iopub.status.idle":"2