uration":0.01673,"end_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.360028+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.343298+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Transfer-learning effect: +0.0773 weighted-score points from ImageNet pretraining alone\n"]}],"source":["print(f\"Transfer-learning effect: {score_pretrained - score_scratch:+.4f} weighted-score points from ImageNet pretraining alone\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"97191246","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.009548,"end_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.378633+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.369085+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Model C — SegFormer, MiT-B0 by default\n","\n","`SEGFORMER_VARIANT` defaults to **`\"b0\"`**, reversed from the earlier draft of this notebook. A real timed run on this exact dataset came back at roughly **26 minutes per epoch for MiT-B4** at the batch size this GPU's memory allows — a 6-epoch run alone took 156 minutes of training, plus data/calibration/TTA overhead on top. Twelve epochs of B4, as this notebook originally defaulted to, would be 5+ hours for that one model alone, before Models A, B, and D even start. B0 is roughly 4x fewer encoder parameters and was already proven to train in reasonable time in your own earlier run (0.595 on the leaderboard). Set `SEGFORMER_VARIANT = \"b4\"` below only if you have 6+ hours of uninterrupted GPU quota specifically to spend on this one model — it is not the default for a reason.\n","\n","**Gradient accumulation does not reduce wall-clock time.** `GRAD_ACCUM_SEGFORMER` only matters for B4: it keeps the effective batch size reasonable without running out of memory, by stepping the optimizer every few micro-batches instead of every one — but the same number of forward/backward passes still run every epoch either way. It buys memory headroom, not speed. If B4 is too slow, lowering `EPOCHS_SEGFORMER` is the only lever that actually helps; accumulation won't.\n","\n","The classification head here is built by pooling the segmentation logits themselves (`torch.amax` over the spatial dimensions, per class) rather than tapping into the encoder's internal hidden states. This is a deliberate simplification: it only depends on `SegformerForSemanticSegmentation(...).logits`, the exact call already proven working in your own executed runs — avoiding a dependency on internal API details that can't be verified without running this on real hardware.\n","\n","Discriminative learning rates: the decode head's final classifier layer was reinitialized from ADE20k's 150 classes down to 4 (`ignore_mismatched_sizes=True`), so it needs a higher LR than the pretrained encoder to catch up within a short fine-tune."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":27,"id":"968d6423","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.399252Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.398911Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.405684Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.40502Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019307,"end_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.40744+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.388133+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["class SegFormerWithClassifier(nn.Module):\n","    def __init__(self, model_name, num_classes):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.base = SegformerForSemanticSegmentation.from_pretrained(\n","            model_name, num_labels=num_classes, ignore_mismatched_sizes=True\n","        )\n","        self.classifier_head = nn.Sequential(\n","            nn.Linear(num_classes, 64),\n","            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),\n","            nn.Linear(64, num_classes),\n","        )\n","\n","    def forward(self, pixel_values, target_size):\n","        seg_logits = self.base(pixel_values=pixel_values).logits\n","        seg_logits = nn.functional.interpolate(seg_logits, size=target_size, mode=\"bilinear\", align_corners=False)\n","        pooled = torch.amax(seg_logits, dim=(-2, -1))\n","        cls_logits = self.classifier_head(pooled)\n","        return seg_logits, cls_logits\n","\n","\n","def segformer_forward(model, images):\n","    rgb_images = images.repeat(1, 3, 1, 1)\n","    return model(rgb_images, target_size=(HEIGHT, WIDTH))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":28,"id":"105c51dc","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.426972Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.426399Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.431094Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.430392Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.01578,"end_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.432619+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.416839+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["SegFormer variant: b0 | nvidia/segformer-b0-finetuned-ade-512-512\n"]}],"source":["SEGFORMER_VARIANT = \"b0\"\n","SEGFORMER_MODEL_NAMES = {\n","    \"b0\": \"nvidia/segformer-b0-finetuned-ade-512-512\",\n","    \"b4\": \"nvidia/segformer-b4-finetuned-ade-512-512\",\n","}\n","SEGFORMER_MODEL_NAME = SEGFORMER_MODEL_NAMES[SEGFORMER_VARIANT]\n","print(\"SegFormer variant:\", SEGFORMER_VARIANT, \"|\", SEGFORMER_MODEL_NAME)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":29,"id":"8489e778","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.452206Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.451642Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-11T19:55:19.085944Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-11T19:55:19.085044Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.646384,"end_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:19.087804+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-11T19:55:17.44142+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"model_id":"f47d0c05c0fa4f08b757903cf412c058","version_major":2,"version_minor":0},"text/plain":["config.json:   0%|          | 0.00/6.88k [00:00<?, ?B/s]"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"n